macOS browser coverage uses `macos-26-intel` for WebKit and Chromium, including
extended scenarios. Its contract is the macOS/browser behavior; the ARM workspace
and real native app/CLI checks retain `macos-latest`. Keep artifact labels and
per-OS collectors aligned with the actual selected image. Avoid coupling browser
admission to scarce ARM capacity needed by native builds. A job that never obtains
a runner has no test result; preserve its infrastructure failure separately.
UI coverage and reports require one complete attempt, so recover that workflow
as a whole when an unallocated producer prevents its current-attempt evidence.

ASan owns one reviewed dated nightly in the sanitizer workflow environment.
The producer installs that exact toolchain with `rust-src` once, verifies its
installed manifest date against the declaration and fingerprints `rustc` and
Cargo through that explicit toolchain before restoring the existing cache cohort.
Do not resolve a floating nightly or infer the compiler from an active default:
calendar changes otherwise invalidate reusable dependencies without source changes.
Upgrade this CI toolchain dependency through a reviewed PR with the full native
Linux union and real clean/use-after-free controls on all eight runners; a local
stable archive-protocol fixture does not qualify instrumentation or a cache hit.

ASan's archive producer admits two Cargo compiler jobs, including LLVM jobserver
work, on the hosted Linux runner. Apply this bound only at the compile step after
test("macOS browsers, Health and backend use Intel while Rust and native retain ARM", () => {
  const ui = read("e2e-ui.yml");
  const job = id => workflowJob(ui, id);
  const health = readFileSync(new URL("../../.github/workflows/check-health.yml", import.meta.url), "utf8");
  const rust = readFileSync(new URL("../../.github/workflows/ci.yml", import.meta.url), "utf8");
  const native = readFileSync(new URL("../../.github/workflows/hidden-contacts-native.yml", import.meta.url), "utf8");
  assert.match(job("desktop"), /operating_systems: '\["macos-26-intel"\]'\n      shards: '\[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\]'\n      shard_total: 8/);
  assert.match(job("desktop-windows"), /operating_systems: '\["windows-latest"\]'\n      shards: '\[1,2,3,4\]'\n      shard_total: 4/);
  assert.match(job("portable-shards"), /runs-on: macos-26-intel/);
  assert.match(job("portable"), /name: Portable UI \(macos-26-intel, webkit\)/);
  assert.match(job("chromium-extended"), /os: \[ubuntu-24.04, macos-26-intel, windows-latest\]/);
  assert.match(job("portable-evidence"), /chromium-evidence.mjs collect-artifacts/);
  assert.match(job("reports"), /chromium-evidence.mjs render-artifacts/);
  assert.match(health, /os: \[ubuntu-latest, macos-26-intel, windows-latest\]/);
  assert.match(workflowJob(rust, "checks"), /runs-on: ubuntu-latest/);
  for (const id of ["macos-native", "macos-remaining-build", "macos-remaining-tests"])
    assert.match(workflowJob(rust, id), /runs-on: macos-latest/);
  assert.match(workflowJob(rust, "checks-macos"), /runs-on: ubuntu-latest/);
  assert.match(native, /os: \[ubuntu-24.04, windows-2022, macos-latest\]/);
  assert.match(workflowJob(read("e2e-backend.yml"), "backend-platform"), /os: \[windows-2022, macos-26-intel\]/);
});
