# Messaging media presentation research

Date: 2026-11-20. Scope: compact expression messages and outgoing photo presentation. Research only; no product edits or tests performed.

## Verified first-party findings

- **Inline emoji and standalone stickers are distinct presentation categories.** Telegram describes custom emoji as small animated items inside text, and its API models them as message entities that refer to downloadable documents. A resource-backed image therefore does not require a file-card presentation. This does not mean Telegram renders all standalone stickers at text size. Sources: [Telegram FAQ](https://telegram.org/faq#stickers-emoji-and-reactions), [custom emoji API](https://core.telegram.org/api/custom-emoji).
- **Transport state is not one universal “sent” state.** Signal distinguishes sending, accepted by its service, recipient delivery, and read receipt. Its service-acceptance semantics must not be transplanted into a serverless messenger. Sources: [Signal message status](https://support.signal.org/hc/en-us/articles/360007320751-How-do-I-know-if-my-message-was-delivered-or-read), [sending troubleshooting](https://support.signal.org/hc/en-us/articles/360009303072-Troubleshooting-sending-messages).
- **Mature apps do retain meaningful media controls.** Signal Desktop renders a download control when media needs downloading; pending media can show a circular progress/cancel control. Its attachment status hook distinguishes download-needed, downloading, and ready-to-show states. These controls are conditioned on actual state. Consequently, “all mature IM apps avoid overlays/progress” would be false. Sources pinned to the observed official repository revision: [image presentation](https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop/blob/01e59719454fec204b3f7902fb663d68419848c9/ts/components/conversation/Image.dom.tsx), [attachment status icon](https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop/blob/01e59719454fec204b3f7902fb663d68419848c9/ts/components/conversation/AttachmentStatusIcon.dom.tsx), [status hook](https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop/blob/01e59719454fec204b3f7902fb663d68419848c9/ts/hooks/useAttachmentStatus.std.ts).
- **Photos are conversation content.** Apple's official Messages guide describes photos, videos and animated GIFs being viewable in the conversation, including grouped photo stacks and captions. The official indexed excerpt was retrieved; direct page requests returned HTTP 429, so this research does not infer exact Apple thumbnail dimensions or upload affordances. Source: [Apple Messages image guide](https://support.apple.com/en-gb/guide/messages/ichtb967d30b/mac).

## Application to this user's explicit preference — design inference

1. Use the user's requested compact expression treatment rather than copying Telegram's larger standalone-sticker convention. Render the selected animation/artwork in a text-scale message layout; keep fallback, selected preview and durable artwork at the same geometry. Preserve original artwork and transport compatibility.
2. Render outgoing photos as bounded, aspect-preserving thumbnails. A photo remains naturally larger than a text glyph; consistency means the message frame, status location and interaction model, not squeezing photographs to one text line.
3. Remove the large translucent file-transfer capsule from outgoing sticker/photo artwork. Reuse the compact message footer for waiting/failure/receipt state. Keep detailed byte progress in an existing detail surface or retain it for real file cards, instead of introducing another always-visible panel.
4. Preserve useful incoming-media download, consent, unavailable and retry states. A readable local preview is not evidence of recipient delivery; 100% byte progress is not a read receipt. Do not infer that a peer is offline solely from zero byte progress.
5. Display the exact selected artwork immediately when a bounded preview exists. Handoff to the durable source should retain geometry and avoid replaying preparation. Do not remove limits to solve large-image preview gaps; use bounded thumbnail production if the existing owner supports it.
6. Preserve the current preview owner limits unless separately measured: 3 MiB per preview, 12 MiB total, eight entries, 30-second lifetime, and ownership-based URL reclamation. Keep fast progress subscriptions isolated from the message list. Local owners: `frontend/src/store/outgoingMediaPreviews.ts`, `frontend/src/store/transfers.ts`.
7. Preserve Mesh Talk's explicit delivery contract: `DeliveryFooter` currently treats an attachment receipt as receipt of the card, not download/read. Styling unification must not silently redefine this authority.

## Acceptance evidence to obtain during implementation

- Sender preparing / queued / waiting / transferring / complete / failed + retry: no obscuring capsule, no fake 0% or premature completion, no text-to-large-card layout switch.
- Sticker fallback → exact selected preview → durable animation: compact stable geometry, no resource/identity regression after pack removal or account switch.
- Portrait / landscape / square photo: bounded aspect-preserving thumbnail, useful pending state when dimensions/bytes are unavailable, preserved enlarge/save controls.
- Incoming download / unavailable / permission declined / protected / read-only history: meaningful distinct states remain accessible.
- Browser assertions and a bounded visual pass on wide/narrow layouts, light/dark/wallpaper and reduced motion. Exact sizes and footer composition are this product's design choices, not universal IM standards.

